    # ===========================
    # MEISHODO TALISMANS
    # ===========================

    ^"Meishōdō Talisman System" DEF {
        # Optional detailed rules for meishōdō talismans.
        # If used, replaces the second paragraph of the Iuchi Meishōdō
        # Master's school ability with: "You can sustain a number of
        # meishōdō talismans up to your school rank. If you create one
        # or more in excess of this limit, you must choose a number up
        # to your school rank and release the spirits in the rest."

        # USING MEISHODO TALISMANS
        # A character carrying a meishōdō talisman can perform any
        # invocations sealed within it. They make a check to activate
        # using their skill ranks and the sealed spirit's ring value in
        # place of their own. They still keep dice equal to their own ring.

        # CREATING MEISHODO TALISMANS
        # A member of the Iuchi Meishōdō Master School or who has
        # completed the Student of Names title can create a talisman
        # by completing the Seal in an Object social objective during
        # an otherworldly encounter. This seals a spirit within the object.

        # TECHNIQUES CONTAINED
        # Creator chooses one invocation matching the element of the
        # highest ring of the sealed spirit. Rank cannot exceed the
        # spirit's highest ring value. If two or more rings are tied,
        # creator chooses one. If spirit is Tainted, creator may instead
        # choose one mahō technique with the same requirements.

        # STABILITY
        # Stability = creator's excess momentum from Seal in an Object
        # + creator's ranks in Design - spirit's ranks in Scholar skill
        # group (or Theology if it has individual skills). Minimum 1.
        # If stability reaches 0, spirit shatters the talisman and is
        # unleashed on the world.

        # LOSING STABILITY
        # - Talisman gains Damaged quality: stability -1.
        #   Gains Destroyed quality: stability reduced to 0.
        # - Technique from talisman would cause Afflicted condition:
        #   wielder does not suffer Afflicted, but stability -1.
        # - Activating a technique, wielder drops one or more ring dice
        #   containing (st)(op): stability -1.
    }

