            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 3 Survival (Air) check to find a path to civilization through impenetrable desert, dense forest, or treacherous mountains. On the ocean, use Seafaring instead of Survival."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you find a sign of the nearest habitation of humans or other sentient beings and can determine the direction to reach it."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op)+: Learn one key detail about the inhabitants per (op)(op) spent: culture/national affiliation, means of subsistence, commonly used technologies, or time since they last passed your location. (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Analyze approach by 1 until end of next scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 111)
    ^"Shadow of Days" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Ritual"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a downtime activity, you may make a TN 4 Culture (Earth) check to calculate distance between two locations. You must have knowledge of stars visible at each location or shadow lengths at certain hours. If you have visited both locations, TN is 2 instead."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you determine the distance between the two locations as the crow flies in li, from which you can estimate travel days. Does not necessarily account for all obstacles."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed and have access to a map, create a more accurate estimate accounting for known obstacles. (op)(op): Reduce TN of checks using the Recall approach by 1 until end of next scene. (op)(op)(op): Accurately predict a future celestial phenomenon in one or both locations."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TECHNIQUES - SHUJI
    # ===========================

    # -- Air Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 112)
    ^"Cunning Omission" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a Sentiment (Air) check targeting another character. TN equals target's focus minus their current strife (minimum 1)."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target slips up and admits something they were concealing from you. If your target was not concealing anything, you know this fact with certainty."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op)+: If you succeed, your target receives 2 strife per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 113)
    ^"Entice with Offerings" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 3 Commerce (Air) check targeting another character. You must give up something the target wants: a physical object or a concession that adds 2 momentum points to the target's current objective."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you distract your target for one round; they cannot add momentum to their social objectives. Persists for one round plus one additional round for every two bonus successes."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Instead of being unable to add momentum, when the target would add momentum to their social objectives, those points are added to one of your social objectives instead. Target is unaware."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 113)
    ^"Trader's Intuition" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Air"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a Commerce (Air) check targeting an object you can observe. TN is 2, or 4 if the object has the Forbidden item quality."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you assess the target, learning its monetary value and rarity."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): You know a place (which you have visited) where you could sell the object for more money than it is worth in your current location."
        }
    }

    # -- Earth Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 114)
    ^"Cite the Facts" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action check, you may make a Scholar skill (Earth) check targeting another character using a relevant Scholar skill. TN equals target's focus minus their current strife (minimum 1)."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target suffers the Silenced condition unless they choose to gain strife equal to your ranks in Command, plus one for every bonus success."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If you succeed, add one bonus success for each reserved die you have. (op)(op)+: Choose one additional target with a focus lower than the original target's per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 114)
    ^"Solidify Gratitude" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Earth"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a TN 2 Courtesy (Earth) check targeting another character. Can only target a character who has accepted a gift from you this scene or has completed a social objective to which you contributed momentum."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you gain the Ally (Target's Name) [Water] advantage unless your target chooses to forfeit glory equal to the rarity of the gift you gave or the number of momentum points you contributed to their objective."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): You learn your target's reason for pursuing their social objective. (op)(op): You gain your target's assistance on the next check you make until end of scene."
        }
    }

    # -- Fire Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 114)
    ^"Glorious Entrance" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Fire"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you enter a scene, you may make a Performance (Fire) check. TN equals the difference between the glory rank of the character in the scene with the highest glory and your glory rank (minimum 1)."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, reduce the TN of Scheme and Support action checks you make by 1. Persists for one round plus one additional round for every two bonus successes."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op)+: When you receive a glory award, increase the amount by 1 plus 1 per additional (op)(op) spent this way. (op)(op): You gain the Emboldened condition."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 114)
    ^"Incite Wrath" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Fire"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Scheme or Support action check while riding a mount or while you have an animal companion at range 0-1, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "(op)(op)+: Your mount or animal companion immediately performs a Strike action targeting one character within range of one of its readied weapons. The damage it deals increases by 1 per (op)(op) spent this way."
        }
    }

    # -- Water Shūji --

    # source stat block (page 115)
    ^"Call to Ride" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you can make a TN 1 Survival (Water) check targeting your mount or animal companion, provided it is within range 5 of you."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your mount or animal companion immediately moves up to 2 range bands toward you, plus 1 additional per two bonus successes. If it is a mount and ends at range 0, you can immediately mount it."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Increase TN of Attack action checks targeting you and your mount/companion by 1 until end of your next turn. (op)(op): If you perform a Maneuver action after mounting, you may move up to 2 range bands instead of 1."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 115)
    ^"Complementary Experience" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Command (Water) check targeting one other character in the scene."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, your target has your assistance on the next check they make (persists until end of your next turn). If you succeed, your target may grant you assistance on the next check you make (persists until end of your next turn)."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Choose one skill in which you have 0 ranks and your target has 1 or more ranks. When you grant assistance, you count as being trained in that skill until end of scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 115)
    ^"Horse Whisperer" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 3
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a Courtesy (Water) or Survival (Water) check targeting a horse or other equine creature that can see or hear you and trusts you. TN equals target's vigilance."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, you make a wordless request to the target which they comprehend and are compelled to fulfill. If what they do is helpful to an action, that action counts as having assistance. Cannot request the impossible. If the horse becomes injured or harmed, it breaks the trust and becomes immune to this shūji."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op)(op): Give the target the Loyal Steed ability (it can be ridden by a silhouette 2 or lower rider) until end of scene."
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 115)
    ^"Everyone Has a Price" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 4
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Scheme action, you may make a Sentiment (Water) check targeting another character. TN equals the target's honor rank. You must offer a bribe with koku value equal to the target's intrigue threat rating. Does not work on mindless or inscrutable Otherworldly creatures (GM discretion)."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed and target is a Minion NPC, they accept the bribe and leave the scene. If target is not a Minion NPC, they must accept the bribe unless they receive strife equal to your ranks in Courtesy. If they accept, they must leave the scene, stop opposing you, or seek terms in negotiation."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "(op): If your target is a Minion NPC, they join your side instead of departing."
        }
    }

    # -- Void Shūji --

    ^"Appreciate the Scenery" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Shūji"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Void"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 1
            ^"Activation" STRING "When you make a Support action check targeting another character, if you and the target are in Dangerous, Entangling, Hallowed, Imbalanced, or Obscuring terrain, you may spend (op) as follows:"
            ^"Effects" STRING "Earth or Water (op): You and your target each remove strife equal to your ranks in Composition. Air or Fire (op): You and your target gain the Emboldened condition. Void (op): You and your target gain the Centered condition."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW INVOCATION
    # ===========================

    ^"The World is Not Heavy" DEF {
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Invocation"
            ^"Ring" STRING "Water"
            ^"Rank" INTEGER 2
            ^"Activation" STRING "As a Support action, you may make a TN 3 Theology (Water) check targeting yourself or a living creature you are touching with your bare hands."
            ^"Effects" STRING "If you succeed, the target can carry items with maximum combined silhouette value equal to their own silhouette plus 1. Their armor loses the Cumbersome quality while worn. If the target is a steed, the maximum combined silhouette value of riders it can carry increases by 2 (no individual rider may exceed what the steed can normally carry). Persists for the duration of the scene."
            ^"Opportunities" STRING "Water (op)+: Increase max combined silhouette of items the target can carry by 1 per (op) spent. Water (op)(op): Another equipped item the target has loses the Cumbersome quality. Water (op)(op): Increase max combined silhouette of riders the steed can carry by an additional 2."
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW TITLES
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 134)
    ^"Animal Handler" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "GM, after character has tamed and trained a suitable animal (minimum: successful Survival check as downtime activity with TN equal to animal's combat conflict ranks)"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 0
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 24
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Instinctive Command: After you perform an action, you may receive 2 fatigue to have any number of your animal companions each take an action that shares a type with your action (still limited to one action of each type per round)."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Trade Skills (skill group), Martial Arts [Unarmed] (skill), Medicine (skill), Sentiment (skill), = Call to Ride (shūji, technique), = Incite Wrath (shūji, technique), = Touchstone of Courage (shūji, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 134)
    ^"Doomhunter" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "The previous Doomhunter, upon their retirement or impending death"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 20
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 28
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Slayer of Immortals: When you perform an Attack action, you can spend (op)+: You attempt to ascertain your target's mortal weaknesses. Target must resist with a Sentiment check; TN equals your ranks in Survival plus (op) spent (Air +2, Fire -2). If target fails, you learn one key clue to defeating it permanently. If you already know how to defeat it, reduce TN of your next check against it by 2."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Skulduggery (skill), Survival (skill), Theology (skill), = Rank 1-2 Rituals (ritual, tech group), = Skulk (ninjutsu, technique), = Soul Sunder (kata, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 135)
    ^"Imperial Peacekeeper" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A member of the Otomo, Miya, or Seppun family with a status of 65 or higher"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 18
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "By Imperial Command: Once per scene as a Support action, choose a number of characters up to your ranks in Command and demand they pull themselves together. Each chosen character removes 3 strife."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Courtesy (skill), Command (skill), Sentiment (skill), = Rank 1-2 Earth Shūji (shūji, tech group), = Cultural Exchange (ritual, technique), = Pillar of Calm (shūji, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 135)
    ^"Interpreter" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "GM, after character has gained initial familiarity with another culture"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 12
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Linguistic Liaison: You learn the languages of the group for which you are an interpreter. The first time you make a check to interact socially with a member of this group each encounter, reduce the TN by 1."
            ^"Special" STRING "A character who has completed this title can be assigned it again for a new group. The new instance counts as a different title."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Social Skills (skill group), Composition (skill), Culture (skill), Government (skill), = Rank 1 Shūji (shūji, tech group), = Cultural Exchange (ritual, technique), = Traveler's Experience (ritual, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 136)
    ^"Scarlet Banners Ranger" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A leader within the White Horde of status 55 or higher"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 24
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Master of the Lariat: When you make a Martial Arts [Melee] or Martial Arts [Ranged] Attack action check using a Snaring weapon, add 1 kept skill die set to (su)(op)."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Trade Skills (skill group), Government (skill), Sentiment (skill), = Rank 1-2 Kata (kata, tech group), = Cunning Omission (shūji, technique), = Thunderbolt Style (kata, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 136)
    ^"Student of Names" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A shugenja trained in Iuchi's method with status 55 or higher"
            ^"Other Requirements" STRING "Must be capable of performing invocations and cannot be a member of the Iuchi Meishōdō Master school"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 5
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 12
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Meishōdō Secrets: You are learned in the Way of Names and can wield meishōdō. Grants new options in Otherworldly Encounters. You can sustain one meishōdō talisman of your own creation. If you create a second, you must choose one and release the spirit within it."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Command (skill), Culture (skill), Survival (skill), Theology (skill), = Rank 1 Invocations (invocation, tech group), = Spiritual Survey (ritual, technique), = Threshold Barrier (ritual, technique)"
        }
    }

    # source stat block (page 137)
    ^"White Guard Veteran" DEF {
        APPLIES TO [^"Samurai"]
        PROPERTIES {
            ^"Type" STRING "Title"
            ^"Assigned By" STRING "A leader within the White Horde of status 60 or higher"
            ^"Status Modifier" INTEGER 10
            ^"Glory Modifier" INTEGER 15
            ^"XP Cost" INTEGER 32
            ^"Title Ability" STRING "Unrelenting and Inevitable: When you receive strife due to the effect of an Otherworldly or Tainted being, reduce the strife by your ranks in Meditation. When another character makes a check to resist an effect of an Attack action you perform (including resisting a critical strike), increase the TN of that check by 1."
            ^"Advances" STRING "Martial Skills (skill group), Courtesy (skill), Command (skill), Survival (skill), Theology (skill), = A Samurai's Fate (shūji, technique), = Stalking Panther Style (kata, technique), = Sudden Downpour Style (kata, technique)"
        }
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW CONDITIONS
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 133)
    ^"Centered Condition" DEF {
        # The character has cleared their mind of distractions and
        # doubts, allowing them to focus on their task.
        # Effects: When the character makes a check, they may remove
        # up to 2 (st) from the roll results.
        # Removed When: At the end of the scene, or after the
        # character benefits from this condition during a check
        # (whichever comes first).
    }

    # source stat block (page 133)
    ^"Emboldened Condition" DEF {
        # The character is filled with the courage to push themselves
        # beyond their normal limits.
        # Effects: When the character makes a check, they may receive
        # 1 fatigue to keep one additional rolled die.
        # Removed When: At the end of the scene, or after the
        # character benefits from this condition during a check
        # (whichever comes first).
    }

    # source stat block (page 133)
    ^"Possessed Condition" DEF {
        # Willingly or unwillingly, the character has come under the
        # power of a supernatural being.
        # Effects: When Possessed, the spirit states its goal. Character
        # can ignore the goal but receives 2 strife at the end of each
        # scene in which they fully disregarded it. When Compromised,
        # character must unmask and then attempt to pursue the goal
        # until end of scene.
        # When making a check while Possessed, character can use the
        # spirit's skill ranks in place of their own. If the spirit knows
        # invocations or other techniques, the character can use each
        # of these techniques once per scene.
        # Removed When: After spending a scene pursuing the spirit's
        # goal, character can make a Meditation (Void) check with TN
        # equal to the spirit's focus. If successful, Possession ends.
        # Also removed via Dispel Possession social objective, or the
        # spirit can choose to end it at any time.
    }

    # ===========================
    # NEW DEMEANOR
    # ===========================

    # source stat block (page 140)
    ^"Compassionate Demeanor" DEF {
        # Reflects Jin/Compassion virtue.
        # Fire +2, Air -1, Water -1 for social checks.
        # Common Way of Unmasking: Hasty Action (act without thinking).
    }
}
